IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part IV: reg 77.994, Pilot Project No. 23, additional hours of insurable employment for claimants in areas
-- affected by natural disasters. Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt.
-- The text is an unofficial rendering; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- The project is spent (claims made until July 19, 2025). The text refers three times to "the day on which this section comes into force" and never states it: it is an input.
-- Relations (Hohfeld): a claimant referred to in (2)(a) or (2)(b) holds a claim to 300 additional hours in the qualifying period (the Commission bears the duty); (4)(a) and (b) take that claim away
-- from a claimant who has already had it for a previous claim.
-- The postal codes are compared as the text writes them, with the single space (T0E 1E0, T0E 0C0 and R0B 1C0): a code written otherwise is not the same string (fork F-reg77.994).

§ `Regulations Part IV - Pilot Project to Provide Additional Hours of Insurable Employment to Claimants in Areas Affected by Natural Disasters`

§§ `Reg 77.994(1) - purposes`

-- src:1599 | 77.994 (1) Pilot Project No. 23 is established for the purpose of testing
-- src:1600 | (a) the effectiveness of a one-time credit of additional hours of insurable employment in mitigating the impact of evacuations due to natural disasters on the benefits payable to claimants under Part I of the Act; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(1)(a) (src:1599-1600)
`reg 77.994(1)(a) the first purpose of Pilot Project No. 23` MEANS
    "the effectiveness of a one-time credit of additional hours of insurable employment in mitigating the impact of evacuations due to natural disasters on the benefits payable to claimants under Part I of the Act"

-- src:1601 | (b) the effectiveness of using postal codes to identify the claimants to whom that credit should apply.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(1)(b) (src:1601)
`reg 77.994(1)(b) the second purpose of Pilot Project No. 23` MEANS
    "the effectiveness of using postal codes to identify the claimants to whom that credit should apply"

§§ `Reg 77.994(2) - who is referred to`

-- The postal codes: T0E 1E0, T0E 0C0 or R0B 1C0.
-- src:1602 | (2) Pilot Project No. 23 applies in respect of every claimant who, at the time of making an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act, is ordinarily resident in an area with the postal code T0E 1E0, T0E 0C0 or R0B 1C0 if
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(2) (src:1602)
GIVEN `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the postal code of the area in which the claimant is ordinarily resident at the time of making the initial claim` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` IF
        `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act`
    AND (   `the postal code of the area in which the claimant is ordinarily resident at the time of making the initial claim` EQUALS "T0E 1E0"
         OR `the postal code of the area in which the claimant is ordinarily resident at the time of making the initial claim` EQUALS "T0E 0C0"
         OR `the postal code of the area in which the claimant is ordinarily resident at the time of making the initial claim` EQUALS "R0B 1C0")

-- (a) a benefit period beginning no earlier than July 21, 2024 and no later than the day before the day on which this section comes into force is established in respect of the claim and does not end
-- in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act before the day on which this section comes into force.
-- src:1603 | (a) a benefit period beginning no earlier than July 21, 2024 and no later than the day before the day on which this section comes into force is established in respect of the claim and does not end in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act before the day on which this section comes into force; or
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(2)(a) (src:1603)
GIVEN `the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit period is established in respect of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the benefit period ended in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE -- out of range: s 10(8)(d) of the Act (piece ei1)
      `the day on which this section comes into force` IS A DATE -- the text does not state it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` IF
        `the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes`
    AND `a benefit period is established in respect of the claim`
    AND `the day on which the benefit period begins` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2024 7 21)
    AND `the day on which the benefit period begins` BELOW `the day on which this section comes into force`
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the benefit period ended in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act, if it did`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST ended THEN ended AT LEAST `the day on which this section comes into force`)

-- (b) the claim is made during the period beginning on the day on which this section comes into force and ending July 19, 2025.
-- src:1604 | (b) the claim is made during the period beginning on the day on which this section comes into force and ending on July 19, 2025.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(2)(b) (src:1604)
GIVEN `the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which this section comes into force` IS A DATE -- the text does not state it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.994(2)(b) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` IF
        `the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes`
    AND `the day on which the claim is made` AT LEAST `the day on which this section comes into force`
    AND `the day on which the claim is made` AT MOST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 19)

§§ `Reg 77.994(3) and (4) - the additional 300 hours`

-- (3) A claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(a) is deemed to have an additional 300 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period for the benefit period referred to in that paragraph.
-- src:1605 | (3) A claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(a) is deemed to have an additional 300 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period for the benefit period referred to in that paragraph.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(3) (src:1605)
GIVEN `the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.994(3) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have` IS
    IF `the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)`
    THEN 300
    ELSE 0

-- (4) A claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(b) is deemed to have an additional 300 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period in relation to the claim unless (a) a benefit period was established
-- for the claimant in respect of a previous claim referred to in that paragraph; or (b) the claimant made a previous claim in respect of which a benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a) was established.
-- src:1606 | (4) A claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(b) is deemed to have an additional 300 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period in relation to the claim referred to in that paragraph unless
-- src:1607 | (a) a benefit period was established for the claimant in respect of a previous claim referred to in that paragraph; or
-- src:1608 | (b) the claimant made a previous claim in respect of which a benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a) was established.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(4) (src:1606-1608)
GIVEN `the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit period was established for the claimant in respect of a previous claim referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant made a previous claim in respect of which a benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a) was established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.994(4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have in relation to the claim` IS
    IF     `the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)`
       AND (NOT `a benefit period was established for the claimant in respect of a previous claim referred to in paragraph (2)(b)`)
       AND (NOT `the claimant made a previous claim in respect of which a benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a) was established`)
    THEN 300
    ELSE 0

§§ `Reg 77.994(5) - what the additional hours count for`

-- The additional hours a claimant is deemed under (3) or (4) to have in their qualifying period are also to be considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of s 28(4) and paragraphs 30(1)(a), 31(c)
-- and 32(2)(c) of the Act and s 35(3) and subparagraph 35(7)(e)(ii) of these Regulations.
-- src:1609 | (5) The additional hours of insurable employment that a claimant is deemed under subsection (3) or (4) to have in their qualifying period are also to be considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of subsection 28(4) and paragraphs 30(1)(a), 31(c) and 32(2)(c) of the Act and subsection 35(3) and subparagraph 35(7)(e)(ii) of these Regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(5) (src:1609)
`reg 77.994(5) the provisions for which the additional hours count as hours of insurable employment` MEANS
    LIST "subsection 28(4) of the Act", "paragraph 30(1)(a) of the Act", "paragraph 31(c) of the Act", "paragraph 32(2)(c) of the Act", "subsection 35(3) of the Regulations", "subparagraph 35(7)(e)(ii) of the Regulations"

-- src:1609 | (5) The additional hours of insurable employment that a claimant is deemed under subsection (3) or (4) to have in their qualifying period are also to be considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of subsection 28(4) and paragraphs 30(1)(a), 31(c) and 32(2)(c) of the Act and subsection 35(3) and subparagraph 35(7)(e)(ii) of these Regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(5) (src:1609)
GIVEN `the hours are additional hours that the claimant is deemed under subsection (3) or (4) to have in their qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` IF
        `the hours are additional hours that the claimant is deemed under subsection (3) or (4) to have in their qualifying period`
    AND elem `the provision` `reg 77.994(5) the provisions for which the additional hours count as hours of insurable employment`

§§ `Reg 77.994(2) to (4) - the additional hours for a claim`

-- (2) to (4) together: a claimant referred to in (2)(a) is deemed to have 300 additional hours (3); one referred to in (2)(b) is deemed to have them unless (4)(a) or (b) takes them away; others have none added.
-- src:1602 | (2) Pilot Project No. 23 applies in respect of every claimant who, at the time of making an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act, is ordinarily resident in an area with the postal code T0E 1E0, T0E 0C0 or R0B 1C0 if
-- src:1603 | (a) a benefit period beginning no earlier than July 21, 2024 and no later than the day before the day on which this section comes into force is established in respect of the claim and does not end in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act before the day on which this section comes into force; or
-- src:1604 | (b) the claim is made during the period beginning on the day on which this section comes into force and ending on July 19, 2025.
-- src:1605 | (3) A claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(a) is deemed to have an additional 300 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period for the benefit period referred to in that paragraph.
-- src:1606 | (4) A claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(b) is deemed to have an additional 300 hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period in relation to the claim referred to in that paragraph unless
-- src:1607 | (a) a benefit period was established for the claimant in respect of a previous claim referred to in that paragraph; or
-- src:1608 | (b) the claimant made a previous claim in respect of which a benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a) was established.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.994(2), reg 77.994(3), reg 77.994(4) (src:1602-1608)
GIVEN `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the postal code of the area in which the claimant is ordinarily resident at the time of making the initial claim` IS A STRING
      `a benefit period is established in respect of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the benefit period ended in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which this section comes into force` IS A DATE -- the text does not state it
      `a benefit period was established for the claimant in respect of a previous claim referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant made a previous claim in respect of which a benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a) was established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` IS
    IF referredToInParagraphA
    THEN `reg 77.994(3) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have` referredToInParagraphA
    ELSE `reg 77.994(4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have in relation to the claim` referredToInParagraphB `a benefit period was established for the claimant in respect of a previous claim referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` `the claimant made a previous claim in respect of which a benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a) was established`
    WHERE
        baseCondition MEANS
            `reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act` `the postal code of the area in which the claimant is ordinarily resident at the time of making the initial claim`
        referredToInParagraphA MEANS
            `reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` baseCondition `a benefit period is established in respect of the claim` `the day on which the benefit period begins` `the day on which the benefit period ended in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act, if it did` `the day on which this section comes into force`
        referredToInParagraphB MEANS
            `reg 77.994(2)(b) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` baseCondition `the day on which the claim is made` `the day on which this section comes into force`
